#Problem APEX 5.1.36

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Integrals)
## DBsection(Antiderivatives (with trigonometric functions))
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## KEYWORDS(indefinite integral, 'initial value problem')
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(3)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('5.1')
## Problem1('36')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric')->flags->set(tolerance => 0.01, tolType => "absolute");

$a = random(2, 8);

$x  = "\pi";
$y1 = random(-5, 5);
$y2 = random(-5, 5);

$f = "$a \sin x";

$C1    = $y1 - $a;
$C2    = "$y2 - $C1 $x";
$f_int = Formula("-$a*sin x + $C1 x + $y2 - $C1*pi");

BEGIN_PGML
Find the function [`f(x)`] described by the given
initial value problem.
[```
  f''(x) = [$f], \qquad f'([$x]) = [$y1], \;\; f([$x]) = [$y2]
```]

    [`f(x) =`] [_____]{$f_int}{30}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_HINT
[```  f'(x) = \int [$f] \, dx = -[$a] \cos x + C_1.
```] 

Find [`C_1`] by setting [`f'([$x]) = [$y1]`].  Then, 

[```
  f(x) = \int \left( -[$a] \cos x + C_1 \right) \, dx 
  = -[$a] \sin x + C_1 x + C_2.```]
  
Find [`C_2`] by setting [`f([$x]) = [$y2]`]. 
END_PGML_HINT

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Since
[```
  f'(x) = \int [$f] \, dx = -[$a] \cos x + C_1.
```]

Find [`C_1`] by setting [`f'([$x]) = [$y1]`].

[```
  \begin{aligned}
    -[$a] \cos [$x] + C_1 &=& [$y1]\\
     [$a] + C_1 &=& [$y1]\\
     C_1 &=& [$C1]
  \end{aligned}
```]

[```
  f(x) = \int \left( -[$a] \cos x + [$C1] \right) \, dx 
  = -[$a] \sin x + [$C1] x + C_2.
```]
Find [`C_2`] by setting [`f([$x]) = [$y2]`].

[```
  \begin{aligned}
    -[$a] \sin [$x] + [$C1] [$x] + C_2 &=& [$y2]\\
     C_2 &=& [$y2] - [$C1] [$x]
  \end{aligned}
```]

Thus, [`f(x) = -[$a] \sin x + [$C1] x + [$C2]`].
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();    

